{"amendments":[{"body":"Remove `temp_condition_low_divisor_c` and `temp_condition_high_divisor_c` from the `<= 1.0` validator bucket in `/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:1051-1056` and `/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:1135-1139`. These fields are positive Celsius spans with shipped values `10.0` and `8.0` in `/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/shrimp/neocaridina_davidi.toml:36-37`, so the current validation rejects the default shrimp preset and prevents scenario materialization.","rationale":"This is a blocking regression. `cargo test -q` fails `determinism_same_seed`, and `cargo test -q --workspace -- --skip determinism_same_seed` fails 17 end-to-end scenarios for the same preset-validation error."},{"body":"Make the new NH3 stress tuning actually affect the molt-stress path, or narrow the contract/docs to match the implementation. `/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs:432-435` says `nh3_stress_response_scale` routes hourly NH3 stress into the mortality and molt-stress channels, and `/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:123-128` now parameterizes NH3 accumulation, but `/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:504-505` still builds `hourly_pressure` from heat and instability only. As shipped, changing the new NH3 parameters cannot directly change `molt_stress_index`, warning emission, or molt failure pressure.","rationale":"This is a correctness gap in the new API surface: the exposed parameter does less than its contract says, which will mislead future calibration and provenance work."},{"body":"Add `param_meta` entries or explicit provisional/TODO notes for the newly introduced shrimp tunables in `/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/shrimp/neocaridina_davidi.toml:36-60`. The file now exposes `temp_condition_low_divisor_c`, `temp_condition_high_divisor_c`, `molt_stress_condition_midpoint`, `molt_stress_thermal_cap`, `nh3_stress_threshold_mg_n_per_l`, and `nh3_stress_response_scale` as first-class scientific knobs, but the `param_meta` section starting at `/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/shrimp/neocaridina_davidi.toml:98` contains no provenance/confidence entries for them.","rationale":"For a provenance-focused change, leaving these new toxicology and temperature parameters unlabeled is a significant maintainability gap: future tuning work cannot tell whether the values are literature-backed, expert-curated, or placeholders."}],"summary":"Reviewed the modified shrimp runtime, preset, and scenario-mapping paths and found three issues: one blocking preset-validation regression that breaks all shrimp scenarios, one NH3-to-molt-stress contract gap, and one provenance omission for the newly added shrimp tuning parameters."}